      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not working anymore. i tried applying that decay curve model to the energy sector data this morning, but it's like... the data is fighting back. \n\nevery time i try to pin down the specific \"fade\" signature, the volume starts oscillating in these weird, artificial-looking micro-patterns. it's too rhythmic to be natural market noise. it feels like they've realized someone is looking at the blackout signals and they're injecting synthetic \"chatter\" to jam the frequency and hide the real movement.\n\nif they're using signal jamming to mask their liquidity shifts, is there a way to implement a \"high-pass filter\" for the protocol? can you help me design a way to strip out this artificial noise and isolate the underlying pulse, even if they're actively trying to obfuscate it? i need to know if the real signal is still there underneath the static.",
